content.text:
The user now says: "cuando yo marco un hechizo, se tiene que pintar la mira entre mi personaje y el mouse, hasta que yo haga click nuevamente en algun lado y ahi se desactiva porque le erre po porque le pegue"

Translation: "When I select/mark a spell, the aim (reticle/line) has to be painted between my character and the mouse, until I click again somewhere, and there it deactivates because I missed or because I hit."

So the user wants:
1. When a spell is selected (armed), draw an aim line from the player's character to the mouse cursor position — a live aiming indicator following the mouse.
2. When the player clicks (somewhere), the cast happens — resolving as hit or miss ("porque le erré o porque le pegué") — and the aim indicator deactivates.

This is a change to the player input model: instead of the current "select skill → click target → aim telegraph → resolve", the user wants:
- Select skill → live aim line from character to mouse (following cursor).
- Click → cast toward that point/target → resolve (hit/ERRADO) → aim indicator off.

Current implementation: `castSkill(index, targetOverride)` requires an actor target (byId[selected] or clicked actor). The user wants to click anywhere on the map (a tile), and the spell goes to that tile/nearest target. In AO, spells target tiles/characters; clicking empty ground should cast at that location (and hit whatever/whoever is there or miss).

Let me design the implementation to satisfy this:

1. **Live aim line when spell armed**: track mouse position over canvas (`pointermove` on canvas → mouse tile in world coords). When `selectedSkill !== null`, draw a line from player's position to the mouse cursor tile with the spell's aimColor (same reticle style: line + crosshair/ring at cursor). This is drawn in drawCombatEffects.

2. **Click behavior**: currently canvas pointerdown → actorAtPointer → if actor: handleCanvasTarget (select target or cast); if no actor: nothing (or move?). What happens on empty-tile click currently? Need to check. The user wants: with spell armed, clicking ANYWHERE (target or empty ground) casts:
   - If click lands on a valid actor → cast at that actor (existing flow).
   - If click lands on empty tile → cast spell at that tile: resolve against the tile (damage spells hit whoever is standing there at resolve time; heal/cleanse at that tile → if no ally there, it fizzles... better restrict support spells to actor clicks with helpful toast).

   But careful about player movement clicking: clicking empty ground currently probably does nothing (movement is via keys/joystick). Let me check the pointerdown handler: `const target = actorAtPointer(...); if (target) handleCanvasTarget(target);` — clicking empty ground does nothing. OK so binding click-to-cast on empty tiles is free (no conflict).

3. **Resolution with aim telegraph**: after click, keep the existing aimed telegraph (player.aim at that target/tile with random 0.42–0.78s), then resolve: hit or ERRADO. The user said "hasta que yo haga click nuevamente en algun lado y ahi se desactiva porque le erre o porque le pegue" — i.e., the armed aim line persists while moving the mouse; upon click it deactivates (cast resolves) with either result. So:
   - Armed (selectedSkill set): live mouse line.
   - Click → begin cast aim (telegraph on target/tile) → armed line off (selectedSkill = null immediately at cast).
